## Interface: 16001
## Title: Social
## Notes: A chat window in the style of a messenger: every message in a bubble, yours on the right, everybody else's on the left with name and class icon. Enter or / opens the line to write in at its bottom, a click on the chat's name there lists the chats to write in. Move and size it in Edit Mode; push the mouse against the screen edge it is docked at and it fills the screen. The game's chat stays next to it; the setting Show the game's chat too hides it. /sane social (or /sane chat) hides this window.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Note_02
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, the game's chat events and the command. First: the other files add to that table.
Social.lua
# The messages: what an event says, and the list of them. Knows no frames
Log.lua
# Sizes and spacing, and what follows from a window's width. Knows no frames
Layout.lua
# The links in a message: tooltip and click
Links.lua
# How much of a message is seen: its own fade, kept on the message. Knows no frames
Fade.lua
# One message in the window
Bubble.lua
# Where you can write right now. Knows no frames
Channels.lua
# The game's own chat: out of sight, and back
Native.lua
# The line you write in: the game's edit box, in our window
Input.lua
# The list behind the chat's name in that line: where to write, what to show, the game's channels
Menu.lua
# The smiley beside that line: raid marks to write, emotes to do
Picker.lua
# The game's own chat channels, the same on every character as wished. Knows no frames
Join.lua
# The full screen's panels around the chat: where they stand, their look
Board.lua
# The second chat of the full screen, above the chat, with its own choice of chats
Feed.lua
# The friends list of the full screen, as the game's
Friends.lua
# The group finder of the full screen, as the game's
Finder.lua
# The window: moved, sized, scrolled
Window.lua
